<title>CHINA: China says 'H' share firms keep tax favours in 97.</title>
<headline>China says 'H' share firms keep tax favours in 97.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-03-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preferential tax treatment accorded nine Chinese companies listed on the Hong Kong stock market will be continued in 1997, the Xinhua news agency said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The nine companies, including Shanghai Petrochemical Co Ltd and Tsingtao Brewery Co Ltd, were all listed as 'H' shares on the Hong Kong exchange, the agency said.</p>
<p>A circular from the Ministry of Finance and the State Administration of Taxation had stipulated that reduced taxes on earnings would be levied on the nine firms in 1997, it said.</p>
<p>It did not say if the preferential tax treatment for the companies would be continued after the end of the year and gave no other details of the firms involved.</p>
</text>
